# P18 Schema Test Project Rules

## Project Structure

### React Version Structure
- src/
  - components/
    - app/ - Global styles and shared components
    - hero/ - Landing page hero section with phone mockup
    - benefits/ - Benefits section with feature cards
    - schemas/ - Schema explanation section
    - pricing/ - Pricing plans section
    - testimonials/ - User testimonials section
    - header/ - Site header with navigation
    - footer/ - Site footer with links
  - assets/
    - images/ - SVG icons and graphics

## Component Patterns

1. **Component Organization:**
   - Each major section has its own directory under components/
   - Components should be exported as default when they're the main component of their file
   - Styled components should be declared before the React functional component

2. **Styling Approach:**
   - Use styled-components for all component styling
   - Leverage CSS variables from GlobalStyles for consistency
   - Create responsive variants using media queries within styled components
   - Use SharedStyles.js for reusable component patterns

3. **Animation Standards:**
   - Use framer-motion for animations
   - Import animation variants from SharedStyles
   - Use motion.div and other motion components for animated elements
   - Keep animations subtle and performant

## Content Guidelines

1. **Text Content:**
   - Primary language: Kazakh
   - Keep text concise and focused on benefits
   - Use consistent terminology for schema-related concepts

2. **Visual Elements:**
   - Use SVG format for all icons and graphics
   - Maintain consistent color scheme using CSS variables
   - Optimize images for web performance

## Code Conventions

1. **React Practices:**
   - Use functional components with hooks
   - Keep components focused on a single responsibility
   - Extract complex logic into custom hooks if needed
   - Use prop destructuring for cleaner component signatures

2. **Styling Conventions:**
   - Name styled components semantically based on their purpose
   - Order CSS properties consistently (layout → box model → typography → visual)
   - Use props for conditional styling
   - Keep media queries with their respective components

3. **File Naming:**
   - Component files: PascalCase.js (e.g., PhoneMockup.js)
   - Utility/helper files: camelCase.js
   - Test files: ComponentName.test.js

## Browser Support

- Support latest 2 versions of major browsers
- Ensure responsive design works on devices down to 320px width
- Progressive enhancement approach for features

## Performance Considerations

1. **Animation Performance:**
   - Use hardware-accelerated properties (transform, opacity)
   - Be cautious with animations on mobile devices
   - Consider using the will-change CSS property for complex animations

2. **Asset Loading:**
   - Optimize SVGs for web use
   - Consider lazy loading for below-the-fold content
   - Minimize bundle size by avoiding unnecessary dependencies 